Description: TPM2-based TOTP authenticator with PCR policies
 tpm2-kira is a command-line tool that provides TPM2-based TOTP (Time-based
 One-Time Password) authentication with Platform Configuration Register (PCR)
 policies for enhanced security.
 .
 The tool can seal TOTP secrets to the TPM using PCR policies, ensuring that
 the secrets can only be accessed when the system is in a trusted state.
 It supports fallback authentication via passwords and can be integrated
 into the boot process for early authentication scenarios.
 .
 Key features:
  * Seal TOTP secrets with TPM PCR policies
  * Generate TOTP codes from sealed secrets
  * Reseal secrets after system updates
  * Integration with initramfs for early boot authentication
  * Support for multiple PCR selections
  * Fallback password authentication
